33afdbfab75249","f73ab87ffc05dd10","f78730f27ce89043","f8252cab854893a0","f867fc7e58a6c15c","f8f74181cd07c768","f95348bca7cdc710","f9e5743dc69eeff2","fac74beac57f46a2","fadb5cda7e72dcfd","fb218f2cdc349127","fb28b204e283a74a","fb2efe0693523915","fbd5c80e6bf44b69","fbedfad3e7bd73b7","fc7ab441f3eac602","fcc57f5ba527ddcc","fd14aba2603b8c1f","fdaf05019f3a88d6","feadaadcb388e56a","ff6b89255f7326cf","ff774ca17bdd456c"],"groups":["ebf9c262bc5d687d","79fa3c3913f14181","64efcb45f0345ed2","c704137b2da2dadd","c6c0cd14878ebd3e","29c50a60d167d1d7","11176d79da21d3bf","a74d7decfbfefa52","10c99c29118715d9"],"findings":"Findings are ranked by benefit. I ran the findings test file on the clone before and after one trial edit, and restored the file afterwards. `git status` shows only `node_modules`, so the snapshot is intact.\n\n1. **Drop the plain `1. Title` heading heuristic** (`src/findings.ts`, `plainTitle` and its call in `scan`, about 17 lines, plus its test). **Verified:** with the call disabled, the only failing test is \"a plain `1. Title` line is a heading only when…\". No fixture in `test/fixtures/reports/` contains a plain numbered title, so the rule is covered only by its own synthetic test. The author's own risk note says heuristics can mislabel reports, and this is the most speculative of the three heading forms. The cost is that reports whose section titles are plain `1. Title` lines would stop taking a section number. That trade-off is the author's call. Size: small deletion. Checked: yes, as a trial.\n\n2. **Read each review's notes once in `--decide`** (`src/commands/reviews.ts:70` and `:89`). `holders` calls `readReviews` per commit to find the review, then `holders.flatMap(readReviews)` reads the same notes again to find the report. Keeping the per-commit results and reusing them removes a second `git notes` read per holder. Size: about 3 lines. **Read** only, not applied.\n\n3. **Move the time sort into `orderDecisions`** (`src/commands/reviews.ts` near the `decisions on this review` loop, and `src/html/data.ts` in `pageReviews`). Both call sites sort by `at` and then call `orderDecisions`. Sorting by time inside `orderDecisions` (refless entries keep time order) gives one ordering rule in one place, and the callers stop having to know it. Size: small. **Read** only.\n\n4. **Share the bullet-marker check** (`isBullet` and the marker test in `itemText`). These are two copies of the same `-`, `*`, `+` followed by space or tab rule. Using one helper removes a duplicate. Size: about 3 lines. **Read** only, and minor.\n\n5. **No change suggested for `stripLabel`.** It makes relabelling idempotent for text a reviewer copied from the `reviews` output. That is a real input path, so it earns its place.\n\nPerformance: `labelFindings` is one linear pass, and the 50,000-item and 200 KB-line test ran in about 0.13 s here. No cost concern at realistic sizes.\n\nOverall the change is fairly lean for what it does. The main cost is the heuristic parser, and suggestion 1 is the one that trims it.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
